    "category": "feature",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“They told it to scare the kids. You heard it and took notes.”</em></p><p><strong>The Thing in the Story (1/Soma Break).</strong> As an action, you become exactly what the town is afraid of, for 1 minute. While it lasts: you are invisible to any creature that isn't looking directly at you (a creature that uses its action to search for you, or that you attack, can see you); your Blood-Drinker bite deals an extra 2d6 qliphothic damage; and the first time each turn a creature sees you, it must succeed on a Soul defense check against your DC or be Shaken until the end of its next turn. Creatures that have known you for more than a day are immune to the fright, which is its own kind of sad.</p><p>When it ends, the town adds a line to the story, and the GM decides what.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
